    "exit_rule": "drawer_position >= 0.29 and the block moved < 1 cm from its entry position at the final state",
    "guidance": "Validated reliability: 7/12. Four failures never reached 0.29 m and ended at 0.2116–0.2329 m; another crossed late and then closed to approximately 0 (demo12101). The demo12108 failure ended at 0.0168 m and included 222 IK-unconverged steps. All runs still kept the block within 1 cm. Use selectively when target_pose is reliable and the hybrid prior is specifically wanted: drawer-relative early/pull position with a smooth transition at 90–98% progress to fresh-TCP-relative position near the stop. There is no validated out-of-distribution evidence that this hybrid improves displaced-drawer handling; h02 is the stronger in-distribution choice, and h03 is the documented choice when the independently placed block should anchor the tail. Avoid when progress is noisy/nonmonotone, orientation displacement or block-relative tail alignment is central, branches disagree strongly, or dependable final-open retention is required. Recognize failure by not reaching 0.29 m, regression or re-closing after reaching it, repeated gripper sign changes/closed fingers after opening, TCP returning toward the handle, target/body branch disagreement, block motion, or IK nonconvergence/residual/limit contact. Hand off only after stable near-0.300 m opening, released/open fingers, safe TCP clearance, and an unmoved block; actions 300:440 supervise a fresh-TCP-relative retreat/turn/descent overlap, and both causal frames must be retained."
